      "verified_by": "a_root_off_stays_below_text_size",
      "fine_trace_step": 5,
      "description": "After ordered-list digit scanning advances `off` to the end of the document, this condition checks only `off > beg` before dereferencing `CH(off)` to look for `'.'` or `')'`. When the digit run reaches the document boundary, `off == ctx->size`, so the delimiter probe itself is out of bounds. The patch fixes this exact obligation by inserting `off < ctx->size` before `CH(off)`."
    },
